/// HTTPHandler — Protocol for actors that can serve as an `HTTPServer` handler.
///
/// `HTTPServer start:handler:` accepts an actor in place of a block. The
/// runtime dispatches each incoming request by sending `handle:` to that
/// actor and expects an `HTTPResponse` back — an actor that does not
/// implement `handle:` will fail at the message-send, not at compile time,
/// unless it conforms to this protocol.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// Actor subclass: EchoHandler
///   handle: req :: HTTPRequest -> HTTPResponse =>
///     HTTPResponse new: #{ #status => 200, #body => req body }
///
/// srv := HTTPServer start: 8080 handler: EchoHandler spawn
/// ```
Protocol define: HTTPHandler
  /// Handle an incoming request and return a response.
  handle: request :: HTTPRequest -> HTTPResponse
